<!-- Section 27: On-chip Debugging Unit (OCD) — PDF pages 2026–2031 (manual pp. 2006–2011)

     This section describes the Nexus/IEEE-ISTO-5001 Class 1 on-chip debug interface
     of the V850E2/Px4 (UPD70F3508).  The OCD is accessed exclusively through dedicated
     pins (DCUTRST, DCUTCK, DCUTMS, DCUTDI, DCUTDO, DCUTRDY) using a serial debug
     protocol — it exposes NO memory-mapped control registers visible to the CPU address
     space.  Consequently there are no <peripheral> elements to emit for this section.

     Contents of the six pages:
       27.1  Functional Overview  (debug monitor, hardware/software breaks, RRM, DMM, …)
       27.2  Connection with the On-Chip Debugging Emulator  (pin diagram + Table 27-1)
       27.3  Notes on On-Chip Debugging  (12 operational cautions)

     No register-overview table, no "Register in Detail" subsection, and no hex addresses
     appear anywhere in these pages.  Nothing to extract.
